# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Project name: GraphVista

Tagline: See Algorithms in Action.

Project type: Interactive graph algorithm visualization website.

## Problem statement

Graph traversal algorithms such as Breadth-First Search and Depth-First Search are fundamental concepts in computer science. Students often struggle to understand their execution because the algorithms are usually explained through static diagrams or code alone.

GraphVista addresses this problem by allowing users to create graphs and watch traversal algorithms execute visually, one step at a time.

## Main objective

Create an educational website that helps users understand:

* Graph vertices and edges
* Directed and undirected graphs
* Breadth-First Search (BFS)
* Depth-First Search (DFS)
* Visited nodes
* Traversal order
* BFS queues
* DFS stacks or recursion behavior
* Backtracking
* Connected and unreachable nodes
* Time complexity
* Space complexity

All core functionality must work without requiring an API key, backend, database, or internet connection after the application has loaded and its assets are available.

