# 14. COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS

Create a compact educational card that explains the complexity of BFS and DFS.

For adjacency-list implementations:

BFS:

* Time complexity: O(V + E)
* Auxiliary space complexity: O(V)

DFS:

* Time complexity: O(V + E)
* Auxiliary space complexity: O(V)

Explain:

* V represents the number of vertices.
* E represents the number of edges.
* The time bound assumes the usual adjacency-list representation and a traversal that processes each reachable vertex and edge a constant number of times.
* The O(V) auxiliary-space bound includes visited-state and queue or stack storage in the conventional analysis.

Explain that implementations using an adjacency matrix may have different time complexity, commonly O(V²).

Keep the explanation beginner-friendly.

Do not claim that every graph representation has identical complexity.

